// assets/media/veo_request.ron
// Generation parameters every paid Veo start request sends, read by `asset_baker generate-veo`
// (and shown by its `--dry-run`) before any credential is read. The ledger's `request_started`
// line records them exactly as sent.
//
// Not a secret. Plan docs/plans/2026-11-04-veo-letterbox-bake.md, decision D-6.
//
// - `aspect_ratio`: "16:9", the shape Veo 3.1 Fast returns at 720p. The baker fits it into the
//   square game frame as `catalog/media_style.ron`'s `framing` section says.
// - `duration_seconds`: length of each clip, in seconds.
// - `sample_count`: videos per request; must be 1 (the budget counts one clip per request).
// - `generate_audio`: `None` sends no field, as the 2026-11-04 pilot did, and the service then
//   generates a sound track (the pilot's clip has one). The owner chose to keep sound, which
//   the game may later play when a unit is clicked (Q0043, answered 2026-11-04), so no silent
//   clip is requested. `Some(false)` would ask for a silent clip ($0.08 per second instead of
//   $0.10 at the published 720p rate); `Some(true)` would ask for sound explicitly.
(
    aspect_ratio: "16:9",
    duration_seconds: 4,
    sample_count: 1,
    generate_audio: None,
)
